 "disabledSets": {
  "why": "Parked accent implementations, kept here on purpose. NEVER remove them: they are the casting work for accents the active bank cannot produce, and for the beast tribes / allied societies and NPC archetypes (Garlean, dragon). They are NOT shown in the UI because each needs a model id bound in overridenModelIds.txt ('<id> ; <Name> ; <setKey>') \u2014 the voice-resolution log now prints race/tribe/sex/model for every speaker, so talk to a tribe member, read the model id from the log, add the line, and that tribe is voiced. Enabling is a data change, never a rewrite. NOTE: the jf_/jm_ (Japanese) and zf_/zm_ (Chinese) banks garble English on the v1.0 model \u2014 they are language voices, not English-accent voices \u2014 so any cast using them stays parked.",
